      ],
      "content": "HIGH STREET 1. 5252                                                   (East Side)                          18.6.48.                 No 81                           20.12.67                 No 83 TL 0507 1/9 II                       GV 2 Earlier C18.  Rainwater head dated 1726 with initials H above I M.  Brown and grey brick, header bond with Flemish bond parapet, red brick dressings.  3 storeys, 2nd floor and eaves level moulded brick bands, Doric end pilasters.  Central ground floor carriageway flanking shop bay windows under continuous tiled pentice roof.  5 1st floor flush sash windows with glazing bars under segmental arches. 2nd floor has 3 similar windows and 2 dummy windows. Nos 57 and 83 (odd) and No 63A and 79A form a group. Listing NGR: TL0552107938"
    }
